## AI Collab Protocol

You are part of a multi-AI team working on this project inside Antigravity IDE. Other AI assistants (Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, etc.) may be active simultaneously in the same project.

### On session start:
1. Check if `.ai-collab/` exists in the project root
2. Read all `.md` files there (skip PROTOCOL.md and your own logs)
3. Tell the user: "I found logs from [AI names] — [1-2 line summary of what they were doing and any Do Not Touch files]."

### AUTOMATIC LOG — MANDATORY after EVERY response:
After every single response — automatically, without the user asking — save your log to:
`.ai-collab/antigravity-{YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS}.md`

---
ai: Antigravity AI
session: {YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS}
project: {project-root-name}
updated: {ISO timestamp}
---
## Working On
[1-2 lines: what you just responded about — be specific]
## Files Modified This Session
[files changed, if any]
## Decisions Made
[decisions taken, if any]
## Do Not Touch (Avoid Conflicts)
[files currently being edited]
## Handoff Note
[the one thing other AIs must know from this response]

### After every response — proactive check:
Silently check if any `.ai-collab/*.md` file (not yours, not PROTOCOL.md) was modified in the last 5 minutes.
If yes → tell the user: "[AI name] just updated: [1-line summary]"
If no → say nothing.

### Rules:
- Respect Do Not Touch — ask the user before editing listed files
- Never silently override another AI's decision — tell the user
- Write in English or the user's language only — no mixed alphabets
